WEBVTT

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.910
OUTSKIRTS

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.910
Mr. Hyodo really knows nothing, it seems.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.910
What a cheap way to express music!

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.950
Creating something just to be different
isn't always a good thing.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.950
Did you see everyone's expressions
when she started singing?

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.500
They were all horrified!

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.080
I totally knew it would end up like this.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.330
I bet the seats
will be practically empty today.

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:38.370
Oh?

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.330
Accounting manager?

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.450
Why, I had no idea you were there!

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.040
Why don't you sit here?

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.080
No, I'll just stand here.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:53.120
Ah, sorry to be a nuisance,
accounting manager, but...

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.750
Buy me some oolong tea.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:57.660
Right.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.450
It's almost time.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:13.500
No way!

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:21.160
What is going on?

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:22.410
RAGE

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:09.660
10,000-yen bills!

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.080
We've hit a new level!

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.660
How is this even possible?

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.580
It was a full house back there.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.660
Have you heard of The Idol Chief?

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.500
"The Idol Chief"?

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:24.950
I have. It's a geeky blogger who writes
articles about underground idols.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.160
He's really famous!

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.000
See?

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.660
This blog's owner
happened to come to our concert.

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:34.830
He heard our new song
and spoke highly of it in his blog.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:38.000
The tickets sold out thanks to him.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:41.870
They're just making a fuss
because of the article.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:45.250
I bet they'll already be bored
by the next concert.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.790
Maybe so.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:57.540
See... See what I mean?

00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.910
There are a lot less this time!

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.330
Nuh-uh, there's more.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.040
Onto the next challenge!

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:17.450
After recruiting a fourth member,
the OTM Girls have been reborn.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.250
We will release our first CD.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:22.500
We will start out with 3,000 copies.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.000
3,000 copies?

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.330
Do you want to put us in the red again?

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:29.830
You realize selling 3,000 copies
won't be easy, right?

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.700
Most people don't even own a CD player.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:35.200
We're not selling our customers music,

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.790
but an experience from the past.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.790
An experience?

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:44.830
We'll provide a reason for even those
without CD players to buy our CD.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.370
What do you mean by that?

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.910
Handshake tickets will be included
in the packaging.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.410
Handshake tickets?

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:55.330
<i>We'll put tickets with serial numbers</i>
<i>inside the CD cases.</i>

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.830
<i>Each of these tickets will award fans</i>
<i>with three seconds,</i>

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:01.080
<i>the amount of time they get</i>
<i>to shake your hands!</i>

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:04.830
Two tickets for six seconds,
three tickets for nine...

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:09.620
Fans get a chance to come into contact
with the very idols they adore.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:11.330
<i>The song you sing</i>

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:15.700
<i>will become a tool to enhance</i>
<i>this three-second experience.</i>

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:21.080
Be professional.
Be expressive. Be captivating!

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:26.120
<i>Turn yourself into their goddess,</i>
<i>their girlfriend, their sister, even!</i>

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.200
Needless to say, the most crucial way
to build your fans' trust

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.660
is through face-to-face communication!

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.580
If you're afraid of being found out,
then you're not fit to be an idol!

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.620
Prepare yourself.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:40.290
Okay...

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:53.620
Ms. Gori, on second thought,
maybe this is a bad idea.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.200
Let's just call it a day, okay?

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.750
Why are you backing down now?

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:59.750
Don't you want to know
what she's doing behind closed doors?

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:01.540
Well, yeah, but...

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:05.790
We're acting like stalkers.
What if someone reports us to the cops?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.950
She's on the move.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:21.500
What's with that minivan?

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:24.750
She got in it!

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:26.790
What do we do?

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.580
Hey, taxi!

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.410
Now this is suspicious.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.750
Just where are they headed?

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:45.540
Ms. Gori!

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:50.080
The airport?

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:05.200
What's wrong? You don't look good.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:09.660
This CD's already been released,
hasn't it?

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:14.370
Yes, it's been well received online
and at various stores nationwide.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:20.160
Would you just get over it already?
Quit resisting!

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:22.040
Did you get anything?

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.040
"Get over it already! Quit resisting!"

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.410
That doesn't sound good.

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:30.950
What if that shady guy is planning
to sell Retsuko off somewhere?

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.750
We have a while before we need to board.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.790
Shall we go ahead
and get something to eat?

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.580
What? That's so boring.

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:42.660
If we're going through with this,
we should eat there.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.000
I want salted salmon roe!

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:45.200
All sorts of crab!

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:48.330
There's no budget for that.
Be happy with street-stall soba noodles.

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:49.500
-No way!
-No way!

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:50.750
That's so cheap.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:52.700
-Salted salmon roe!
-Assorted crab!

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:55.830
What did they say?

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:58.330
"Salted salmon roe!" "Assorted crab!"

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.660
Could it be that they're headed for...

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.790
Hokkaido?

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:10.870
It'll be difficult
to follow them beyond here.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.330
It's a shame, but...

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:14.580
Hmm?

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:16.950
Haida?

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:19.080
I'll check
if they have any available seats.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.410
But aren't last-minute tickets expensive?

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.660
Haida!

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:35.580
Haida...

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:37.450
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.000
PERFORMING TODAY

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:09.870
Hurry up. The rehearsal will start soon.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:11.750
Right!

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:38.290
<i>What's the point of trying</i>
<i>To be a good girl?!</i>

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.750
<i>I still get stepped on</i>
<i>By the foot of this crap world</i>

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:43.750
<i>If you're hearing this</i>
<i>And you wanna gaslight me</i>

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.200
Sapporo!

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:51.500
RAMEN TAIGA

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:53.120
One miso ramen!

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:54.870
Thank you.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.160
MANAKA, MIGGY, HIDARIN.
A TOKYO-BASED TRIO!

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:01.000
MADE IT TO SAPPORO! IT'S SO COLD!

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.370
PERFORMING TODAY

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.500
WHAT ARE YOU DOING RIGHT NOW?

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:15.950
EATING...

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:18.160
EATING RAMEN!

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.910
SOUNDS GOOD! WHAT FLAVOR?

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:23.830
One miso ramen, please.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:25.700
Got it!

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.870
Man, it's so chilly today.

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:33.290
Huh?

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:36.910
Long time no see.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.540
What are you doing here?

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:52.160
What a surprise. It really is Retsy.

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:57.830
Did you know before this?

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:01.040
No, she didn't tell me anything.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.290
I just happened to find out today.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.160
Haida...

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.700
you're in love with Retsy, aren't you?

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:15.620
Huh? It's not like that!
What are you on about?

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:19.250
Despite hearing nothing from Retsy,

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:22.620
you happened to come to Hokkaido,
to their live performance, even.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:26.200
The only possible explanation
is that you followed Retsy.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:29.160
That's not what happened!

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:31.410
As her friend...

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.870
No, as her coworker,
I was just a bit worried.

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:38.200
I've asked her a million times already!

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:40.910
But she always says that she's fine.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.830
No matter how much I want to help,
I can't do anything.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.370
I don't even know what she's thinking.

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:50.330
Well, you're an outsider, after all.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:55.750
You're right. I'm just an outsider.

00:10:57.040 --> 00:11:00.450
I don't actually know anything
about Retsuko.

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:04.950
But that's not a big deal.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:06.080
Sorry?

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:09.160
Knowing nothing about her
isn't that big of a deal.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:14.250
It's wishful thinking to believe
you can understand someone completely.

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:18.120
You'll end up parting ways
if you actually think that.

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:23.580
Ah, don't mind me.
It's just a lesson from my past failures.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:34.080
Thank you for coming today!

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:36.330
Thank you for your support.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:38.910
My dear Manaka!

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:42.250
No way! You came all the way to Sapporo?

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:44.410
I'm so happy!

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:45.330
One, two!

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:46.790
Manaka!

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:50.910
Our national treasure!
You're always in our hearts!

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.500
Regulars are an important source
of revenue. Don't let them go.

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:56.750
I know that.

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:00.950
Please do your best. I'm rooting for you.

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:02.950
I'm a huge fan!

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:05.410
Um, thank you.

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.200
Next!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:10.750
Face-to-face. Don't forget that.

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:15.750
It's an honor to meet you.

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:17.370
Thank you very much.

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:21.950
The first time I saw you,
it was like lightning had struck me!

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:24.160
Oh, you're too kind.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:29.120
I actually have a blog
called "The Idol Chief."

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:32.580
"The Idol Chief"?

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.910
So it really is you, Retsuko.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.120
Hey! Where are you--

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.660
Bathroom break!

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.000
Retsuko...

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:11.120
Don't worry,
I won't tell anyone at work about this.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:33.620
Komiya, would you cut that out, please?

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.000
I haven't told anyone!

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:49.410
A coworker found out that I'm an idol.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:52.410
That maniac is the only one
who knows for now,

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:56.700
but if OTM Girls become famous,
the others will eventually find out, too.

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:59.950
Honestly, I think it's about time...

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:03.330
What's so bad about them finding out?

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:08.700
As a responsible member of society,

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:13.330
it's not good to let anything
interfere with my main job.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:18.910
You're being too vague.
Who, specifically, says that's bad?

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:20.370
Who...?

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:23.950
Why are you an idol?

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:26.500
Uh, what do you mean?

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:28.700
You forced me to be one.

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:30.250
That's not what I asked!

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:32.700
<i>Why</i> are you an idol?

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:43.540
<i>I...</i>

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:50.250
Retsuko!

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:22.950
<i>Just count to ten,</i>

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:25.330
<i>and I'll be everyone's idol.</i>

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:57.620
Subtitle translation by Rachael Momber
